# Vercel deployment ignores
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY: Vercel's Python builder auto-detects a uv project whenever it
# sees `uv.lock` + `pyproject.toml` and force-runs:
#     uv sync --active --no-dev --link-mode hardlink --frozen --no-editable
# That frozen uv path fails in the Vercel build. This project deploys
# with plain pip + requirements.txt (see vercel.json "installCommand").
# Hiding the uv-only files from the Vercel build makes the builder fall
# back to `pip install -r requirements.txt`, which is reliable and is
# what the pinned 250 MB-friendly requirements.txt was made for.
#
# NOTE: these files stay in Git and still work for local uv workflows —
# they are only excluded from the Vercel build/upload context.
uv.lock
pyproject.toml

# uv virtualenvs / caches (never uploaded anyway, but be explicit)
.venv
__pypackages__

# Heavy dev / training artifacts not needed by the serverless function.
test_images/
runs/
models/
dataset/
uploads/
outputs/
